  "name": "HSV 1 & 2 IgG ANTIBODY (CSF)",
  "code": "2773",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong>Comments</strong><br>Herpes simplex virus (HSV) types 1 and 2 are members of the Herpesviridae family, and produce infections that may range from mild stomatitis to disseminated and fatal disease. Infections with HSV types 1 and 2 can differ significantly in their &nbsp;clinical &nbsp;manifestations &nbsp;and &nbsp;severity &nbsp;which &nbsp;can &nbsp;range from &nbsp;gingivostomatitis, keratitis, &nbsp;encephalitis, &nbsp;vesicular &nbsp;skin &nbsp;eruptions, &nbsp;aseptic &nbsp;meningitis, neonatal &nbsp;herpes, &nbsp;genital &nbsp;tract &nbsp;infections, and disseminated primary infection. Infection in neonates occur during passage through birth canal and may result in neurological damage.</p>",
